[00:00.000] 作词 : Austin Lunn
[00:01.000] 作曲 : Austin Lunn
[00:03.270]I hate that we have to see the world burn
[00:10.892]for it to be okay to care about it
[00:18.010]And that we must turn
[00:25.512]back the clock to save ourselves.
[00:31.618]I'm running from the end that you're running to,
[00:39.036]planting the saplings you'll one day wander through.
[00:45.605]And as the spruce buds emerge they are immediately consumed
[00:52.738]by the vermin soon enveloped in their delicate cocoon.
[01:01.289]Can you hear the loon over your own voice?
[01:15.304]Can you hear the silence through the noise?
[01:29.601]No answered questions in ceaseless
[01:35.455]Chattering
[01:44.179]Wind through pines and bones rattling.
[02:04.579]Can you hear the loon over your own voice?
[02:18.997]Can you hear the silence through the noise?
[02:32.630]I hate that we have to see the world burn,
[02:40.289]for it to be okay to care about it
[02:47.515]And that we must turn
[02:54.796]back the clock to save ourselves.
[03:01.038]I'm running from the end that you're running to,
[03:08.259]planting the saplings you'll one day wander through.
[03:15.092]And as the spruce buds emerge they are immediately consumed
[03:22.077]by the vermin soon enveloped in their delicate cocoon.
[03:30.519]Can you see the stars beyond the glowing screen?
[03:44.645]Can you see the rot beneath the sheen?
[04:34.578]So some candles flicker and some candles fade,
[04:48.602]Some skin is brittle and parts at the blade
[05:02.673]For the night seems so long but life seems so short
[05:17.901]Like the hull yearns for water at the sight of the port.
[06:14.072]The treetops are broken
[06:20.644]that I saw sprout from the ground.
[06:27.916]But saplings are far too are burdened
[06:34.971]to know the world is burning down.
[06:42.833]Disgraced by the vermin
[06:49.184]who upon their buds fed
[06:56.667]Barren of needles they rot where they stand,
[07:03.406]Like the vapid faces of the bereft walking dead.
[08:06.305]In whose hand is my torch,
[08:09.823]which once lit my way?
[08:13.513]Through valleys and mist into the dawn of day
[08:21.031]We all fade away in memory's rime
[08:28.255]The picture stones details blurred by the passage of time.
